  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-3,-4)$ and $(9,8)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Determine the radius $r$ of the circle.\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3-9)^{2}+(-4-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{288} \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{2}=6\\sqrt{2}\n$$",
